# Cargo runs rustc: the package brings the compiler it was built with.
INSTALL /v0.1.4/demos/rust/Dollyfile-rust 16b0355bc8e05baefcfbd14d551c024f5a369cc702f0d06b74c1736b5300f5d7
# Until Dolly has file locks: rustc's incremental sessions need them.
EXPORTS ENV CARGO_INCREMENTAL 0
# The cc crate's default flags name a target; Dolly's cc has one.
EXPORTS ENV CRATE_CC_NO_DEFAULTS 1
EXPORTS TOOL cargo
EXPORTS FOLDER cargo-licenses /usr/share/licenses/cargo
FILE /usr/share/dolly/builds/cargo.lock

FILE /usr/share/man/cat1/cargo.1
    cargo: Cargo 1.98.1, built inside Dolly; the rust package is its compiler.
    
      cargo build          builds a crate: path and vendored dependencies,
                           build scripts and procedural macros
      target/debug/NAME    runs what it built
    
    cargo run builds and then fails: Cargo replaces itself with the program
    (exec), which Dolly does not have. Crate archives come through the page's
    HTTP broker; crates.io's index needs a relay or a vendored directory. A
    crate that uses libc needs the SDK's copy, in .cargo/config.toml:
      [patch.crates-io] libc = { path = "/opt/rust-sdk/src/libc" }
    Incremental builds are off (CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0). There is no cargo search,
    publish or login. Upstream's book: https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/
